      "reading": "Two scans were each started by a short-lived git parent through bash, the shape of the global pre-commit hook: one in the Claude Desktop coalition at about 09:43:23 (28.25 GiB) and one in the terminal CLI coalition at about 09:44:28 (18.78 GiB, then 24.64 GiB 6.6 s later). The third, started from zsh at about 09:41:21 with a 3.08 GiB git child and 2,934 CPU-seconds, matches a full-history `gitleaks git --redact --log-opts=--all` over agent-ecosystem history mirrors recorded in a session at 09:41. At 09:42-09:43 two sessions recorded tests/test_catalog_freshness_propose.py scratch commits blocked by the global hook; TrackedExplorerSubprocessTests force-adds the generated explorer. PR #181 (merged 10:08 EDT) made test git config hermetic, and this pass confirmed no Gitleaks process starts from that test class now."
    },
    "root_cause": {
      "mechanism": "gitleaks 8.30.1 detect/utils.go filter() calls report.Finding.Redact for every finding, and Redact runs strings.ReplaceAll over Finding.Line, allocating a full copy of the matched line per finding. In git mode a -U0 hunk holds whole lines, so 2,335 findings on the explorer's 12,889,851-byte line retain about 30 GB (28 GiB). dir mode reads files in bounded chunks, so its lines, and its memory, stay small.",
      "probes": "HTML-only staged: --redact exceeded 6 GiB in 14 s; --max-decode-depth=0 still exceeded 6 GiB; without --redact the peak was 0.17 GiB with 2,335 findings; --max-target-megabytes=2 peaked at 0.17 GiB but reported no leaks found with exit 0.",
      "rejected_options": {
        "max_target_megabytes": "Fails open: detectRule skips the whole fragment at debug log level, so the 2,335 findings disappeared and the scan exited 0.",
        "config_path_exclusions": "Not used: a top-level path allowlist skips whole files in both git and dir modes (.gitleaks.toml header), and dir-mode memory was already bounded at 0.13 GiB even for 714 MB with nested worktrees.",
        "gomemlimit": "No effect on the blow-up: with GOMEMLIMIT=4GiB the history scan still crossed the 6 GiB cap (the growth is live findings, not garbage).",
        "kernel_limit": "memorystatus_control(SET_JETSAM_TASK_LIMIT) returned EPERM for an unprivileged caller."
      }
    },
    "method": {
      "harness": {
        "path": "evidence/artifacts/gitleaks-macos-memory-bound-20260924/measure.py",
